            <ArticleTitle>Coronary heart disease in African Americans: primary and secondary prevention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>285-92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary heart disease develops sooner in African Americans than in whites and causes a higher rate of mortality. Because multiple risk factors and risk factor clustering are common, efforts at primary and secondary prevention in this population need to address the total risk-factor profile.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
